---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/write-up.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet"
	pubDate={new Date('August 05 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
	The site uses the astro blog template to display markdown write-ups directly from an Obsidian vault.

	I did this so I can just do write-ups in Obsidian like normal, without having to give thought to how the website is
	parsing them. In the future, I would like to move away from the template styling, and make the site feel more
	personalised, but for now I am pretty happy how it has turned out :)
	</p>

	<p>
		Once I get a search-box and a way to filter the write-ups implemented, I will probably leave the site as-is
		for a while. Maybe I might transform it into more of a personal portfolio in the future, however for now I am
		satisfied with the simple scope of the project.
	</p>

	<p>
		The site isn't meant to be anything overly fancy, and I know in the age of AI programming, trying to compete in
		the space of fancy portfolios is a losing battle. That's why I've settled for this simpler approach, where I am
		doing nice projects by-hand to showcase my education/learning rather than pumping out flashy projects that
		only show I know how to speak to an AI.
	</p>

	<p>
		I hope you enjoy the time on my site, if you notice any bugs or have any suggestions, feel free to let me know
		whatever way you suits you best (but no promises I'll get around to doing anything about it!).

	Have a good day :)
	</p>
</Layout>
